hark ask returned {text:null, end_phrase:null} and ended EARLY while the operator was mid-answer (2026-08-10 ~22:55, radio mode, session_local profile). Operator confirms he was answering; no transcript captured, no end phrase fired. Prior asks in the same session worked. Need: never return silently-null on an armed capture — surface why (mic lease lost? worker restart? STT empty? timeout path returning early) in the JSON (e.g. reason field), and log the capture lifecycle to state dir for post-mortem.

ROOT CAUSE (2026-08-10 23:02): ~/.grok/auth.json was DELETED mid-session (existed 22:20, gone by 22:56). Sequence: tts.ok played -> listen armed -> speech_opened -> stt.request -> stt.response "xAI auth missing" -> ask returned {ok:true, text:null} swallowing the STT failure. Later asks failed harder: OpenAI TTS fallback 429 credit_balance_exhausted -> {ok:false, exit 4}. TWO bugs here: (1) STT provider failure must surface as ok:false + reason, never text:null/ok:true; (2) auth.json deletion suspect: headless grok CLI task (ccc @glm52 job, pid 1559842 running grok -p) may rotate/clobber/remove ~/.grok/auth.json — investigate grok CLI auth lifecycle vs concurrent sessions.
